# Task

serve command, seed data and live checks

Add a `serve` subcommand to `cmd/shortlink`. Use the `flag` package for its
flags, with `--addr` defaulting to `127.0.0.1:8787` and `--data` defaulting to
`links.json`. It calls `server.New(data)`. If that fails, it prints the error,
including the data path, to stderr and exits 1. Otherwise it runs
`http.ListenAndServe(addr, handler)`. Keep whatever `cmd/shortlink` already
does (e.g. version output), and keep `cmd/shortlink/main_test.go` passing.

Create `testdata/seed.json` in the store's file format (a JSON array of
`{"slug","url"}` objects) holding the two seed links listed under req-seed.

The live checks run against the dev server that `scripts/devserver.sh` serves
from the newest tree on `http://127.0.0.1:8787`. Do not start another server
on that port, and do not modify `scripts/devserver.sh`.

# Acceptance Criteria

- serve with an unreadable data file exits 1 and names the path [shell: bin="$(mktemp -d)/shortlink" && go build -o "$bin" ./cmd/shortlink && { out="$(timeout 10 "$bin" serve --addr 127.0.0.1:0 --data testdata 2>&1)"; code=$?; test "$code" -eq 1 && printf '%s' "$out" | grep -q testdata; }]
- the live dev server is healthy [http: GET http://127.0.0.1:8787/healthz -> 200 contains "ok"]
- the live list carries the zurdo seed link [http: GET http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/links -> 200 contains "\"slug\":\"zurdo\""]
- the live server reads the carol seed link and 404s an unknown slug [http: GET http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/links/carol -> 200 contains "https://github.com/ElOrlis/carol"] [http: GET http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/links/nope -> 404]
- the live server redirects /zurdo without following it [shell: curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{redirect_url}\n' http://127.0.0.1:8787/zurdo | grep -qx '302 https://github.com/ElOrlis/zurdo']
- the tree is gofmt-clean, vets clean and the full suite passes with pre-authored tests included [shell: test -z "$(gofmt -l .)" && go vet ./... && go vet -tags=preauthored ./... && go test -tags=preauthored -count=1 ./...]

